2. Web Client
When to use Web Client
- Provides more flexibility
- External API calls(third party services)
- Complex headers, auth, transformations
- Reactive/non blocking systems
- High throughput applications

Example:
webClient.get().uri("http://order-service/orders/12").retrieve().bodyToMono(Order.class)
-------------------
3. Open Feign/ Feign Client
Frameworks handle discovery + load balancing for you
e.g. Spring Boot + OpenFeign

@FeignClient("user-service")
public interface UserClient {
	@GetMapping("/user/{id}")
	User getUser(@PathVariable int id);
}

When to FeignClient
- Crud operations, Simple Service to service calls
- Simplicity, easy integration with Eureka, Load Balancing, Resilience4j	


Feign with or without Discovery Server like Eureka

a) Without Eureka
Feign You can use without discovery servers (Eureka) as below
Example:
@FeignClient(
    name = "order-service",
    url = "http://localhost:8081"
)
public interface OrderClient {
    @GetMapping("/orders/{id}")
    Order getOrder(@PathVariable Long id);
}

b) With Eureka
Feign with eureka:
Example
@FeignClient(name = "order-service")
public interface OrderClient {
    @GetMapping("/orders/{id}")
    Order getOrder(@PathVariable Long id);
}

Advantages of using feign with eureka:
- Dynamic service lookup
- Load balancing
- No hard‑coded URLs
- Better for microservices


